WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "Field Intelligence: a technician's day" (IE, 5:00). The cues are the captions burned into the master (sha256 6ee94d40ce86…),
which sit at the foot, the top or the middle of the picture by scene; read from its frames on 2026-11-13 in four passes and checked by
eye at every gap and every cut-off line. On-screen labels and interface text are not captioned.

1
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.750
Eight in the morning. An experienced AV engineer begins his rounds.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.500
Floor by floor: touch panels, displays, microphones, the room PC, the network.

3
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.250
On a campus like this, the round can take two hours.

4
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.250
Most mornings, almost everything is fine.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.250
That is real expertise, spent confirming that nothing has changed.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.500
Empathia Field Intelligence is built to run on the room's own Windows PC:

7
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.250
a scheduled, read-only collector.

8
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.250
By default, four times an hour, it checks what the room depends on:

9
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:48.000
compute health, cameras, microphones, speakers, displays, the network, and only

10
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.250
the endpoints it is allowed to reach.

11
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.250
It compares what is expected with what it observes.

12
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.000
Each result becomes a structured evidence record:

13
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.750
what was seen, how sure it is, and what it does not prove.

14
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.750
A device that answers a check has not proved that the room works in a call.

15
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.500
Reachable is not the same as working.

16
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.500
In the proposed architecture, those records feed the wider Empathia platform.

17
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.500
Now, engineering the space. Each room becomes a transparent model, built from

18
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.000
declared inputs: dimensions, positions, mounting heights and lenses.

19
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.250
In a four-seat huddle room, one wide camera reaches every seat from a single

20
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.750
preset.

21
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.000
In the boardroom, a far corner seat is 8.5 metres away:

22
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.250
pan, plus 6.8 degrees; tilt, minus 4.7.

23
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.500
In the divisible training room, four corner seats sit only at the edge of each

24
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.500
camera's reach, so the plan calls for more than one preset.

25
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.000
And in the town hall, the model finds the gap before anyone climbs a ladder.

26
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.750
The overflow seats are out of reach. Add one camera, run the plan again, and it is

27
00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.750
valid.

28
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.750
Modeled, not measured: a plan is only as good as its inputs.

29
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.500
Acoustic commissioning is a future capability.

30
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.000
What follows is a simulation.

31
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:17.000
Before any sound could play, the work must be authorized, the room verified empty,

32
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.500
paging and emergency systems protected, the equipment calibrated, and safe levels

33
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.500
approved. Even then, the collector plays nothing.

34
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.500
It reports readiness.

35
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.000
A controlled sweep. Measurement microphones in each zone.

36
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.250
From each recording, an impulse response.

37
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.750
Direct sound first, then reflections, then the decaying tail.

38
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.250
Early energy supports speech; late energy blurs it.

39
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.250
From the decay, a hypothetical reverberation time, band by band, from the

40
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.500
front row to the overflow.

41
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.500
Then a proposal: a delay line of loudspeakers that brings the rear and

42
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.000
overflow close to the level at the front.

43
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.500
Microphone beam coverage would be its own workflow, supported by the manufacturer.

44
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.000
A microphone that is simply present measures nothing.

45
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.000
Ten a.m. A meeting is under way. The collector only ever reads:

46
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.500
no test tones, no camera moves, no recordings.

47
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.500
Ten fifteen. Healthy.

48
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.250
Ten thirty: the touch panel stops answering on its control port.

49
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.000
The finding arrives with its evidence, the likely causes, and the checks to run

50
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.500
first. The cause stays unconfirmed until a person confirms it.

51
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.250
Ten forty-five: still down. The engineer checks the switch port, restores power to

52
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.250
the panel, and makes the call.

53
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.750
Eleven o'clock: the panel answers, but one check could not complete.

54
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.000
Unverified, not healthy.

55
00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:52.250
Eleven fifteen: every required check is conclusive.

56
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.750
Resolved, with the evidence to show it.

57
00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.250
Now the scenario. Even if the whole two-hour round were freed, that is at most 500

58
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.500
hours a year for one engineer, before alerts and upkeep are counted.

59
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.000
It is an illustration, not a result. A pilot will measure the real number.

60
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.500
The point is not to replace engineers.

61
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.750
It is to give their judgment the time it deserves.

62
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.250
Across the campus, Field Intelligence could become a source of evidence for

63
00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:27.750
Empathia Pro, Lite, Search Party and Learn.

64
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.750
The ticket closes with its evidence. And there is time to teach.

65
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.000
The room has a story. Every device. Every signal.

66
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.000
Every failure. Every improvement.

67
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.750
For too long, engineers have spent their days searching for the evidence.

68
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.500
What if the evidence could come to them?

69
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.750
Empathia Field Intelligence.

70
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.750
Know the room. Understand the evidence.

71
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.250
Give engineers their time back.
